cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      # One-class SVM: unusual tree records

      Pilot species: Quercus robur. Question: Which trees have unusual recorded
      age and trunk-diameter classes compared with other Quercus robur trees,
      and where are they? A flag requests data review; it is not a diagnosis of
      health. See 3-bomen_OML_one_class_SVM_checkSQL.sqlnb for source checks.

      The Agent tool runs setup, trains/scores only when needed, and saves every
      scored tree in TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS. It preserves earlier runs. A repeated
      request reuses the latest matching run. The source-change check compares
      the source segment ID, species row count, and MAX(ORA_ROWSCN). ORA_ROWSCN
      can report a later SCN without a relevant data edit, so an unnecessary
      rebuild is possible. Use p_force_refresh='Y' when in doubt. The source
      table has no reliable update timestamp.

      Prerequisites: translated BOMEN_TREES exists, and the density notebook
      has already created TREE_DENSITY_AGENT, TREE_DENSITY_TASK, and
      TREE_DENSITY_TOOL. Run the definition cells in order when no team request
      is active. The final cells rebuild the existing TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM with
      two workers. Do not rerun the density notebook's density-only team cell
      afterward, or it will remove the anomaly worker from the team. APEX
      GET_RESPONSE reads saved map rows by RUN_ID from AGENT_MAP_RESULTS.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 1. Automatic storage setup

      Called by the Agent function. Creates missing tables and map/model views;
      it does not drop saved result rows or the BOMEN_TREES source table.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: "## Q/A\r

      \r

      1- Which Den Haag neighbourhood has the highest tree density (trees per
      km2)?\r

      \r

      2- Which Quercus robur tree records have unusual age and trunk-diameter
      classes?\r

      \r

      3- Which five Den Haag neighbourhoods have the highest tree density
      despite having less than 30% green area?\r

      \r

      4- Do you see anything unusual in my datasets?\r

      \r

      5- Show me the flagged trees on the map"
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: "\r

      BEGIN\r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'DROP VIEW TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS_V';\r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'DROP TABLE TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS';\r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'DROP TABLE TREE_ANOMALY_RUNS';\r

      \    EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'DROP TABLE TREE_ANOMALY_SETTINGS';\r

      END;"
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >-
      CREATE OR REPLACE PROCEDURE prepare_tree_anomaly_storage AS
          v_count NUMBER;
      BEGIN
          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_tables WHERE table_name = 'BOMEN_TREES';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20100,
                  'BOMEN_TREES is missing. Run the translation workflow first.');
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_tables WHERE table_name = 'TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS (
                      RUN_ID               VARCHAR2(32) NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_RECORD_ID     NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SPECIES_NAME         VARCHAR2(254 CHAR),
                      TREE_AGE             NUMBER,
                      TRUNK_DIAMETER       VARCHAR2(50 CHAR),
                      ANOMALY_FLAG         NUMBER(1) NOT NULL,
                      ANOMALY_PROBABILITY  NUMBER,
                      WGS84_LONGITUDE      NUMBER,
                      WGS84_LATITUDE       NUMBER,
                      GEOMETRY             MDSYS.SDO_GEOMETRY,
                      CREATED_AT           TIMESTAMP DEFAULT SYSTIMESTAMP,
                      CONSTRAINT TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS_PK
                          PRIMARY KEY (RUN_ID, SOURCE_RECORD_ID)
                  )~';
          END IF;

          -- Shared map contract: each spatial tool can save GeoJSON rows by RUN_ID.
          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_tables WHERE table_name = 'AGENT_MAP_RESULTS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE AGENT_MAP_RESULTS (
                      RUN_ID         VARCHAR2(32) NOT NULL,
                      FEATURE_ORDER  NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      FEATURE_JSON   CLOB CHECK (FEATURE_JSON IS JSON),
                      CONSTRAINT AGENT_MAP_RESULTS_PK
                          PRIMARY KEY (RUN_ID, FEATURE_ORDER)
                  )~';

              -- Recover map points for runs created before this table existed.
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  INSERT INTO AGENT_MAP_RESULTS
                      (RUN_ID, FEATURE_ORDER, FEATURE_JSON)
                  SELECT r.RUN_ID,
                         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
                             PARTITION BY r.RUN_ID
                             ORDER BY r.ANOMALY_PROBABILITY DESC NULLS LAST,
                                      r.SOURCE_RECORD_ID
                         ),
                         JSON_OBJECT(
                             'RUN_ID' VALUE r.RUN_ID,
                             'SOURCE_RECORD_ID' VALUE r.SOURCE_RECORD_ID,
                             'SPECIES_NAME' VALUE r.SPECIES_NAME,
                             'TREE_AGE' VALUE r.TREE_AGE,
                             'TRUNK_DIAMETER' VALUE r.TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                             'ANOMALY_PROBABILITY' VALUE r.ANOMALY_PROBABILITY,
                             'GEOJSON' VALUE SDO_UTIL.TO_GEOJSON(
                                 MDSYS.SDO_GEOMETRY(
                                     2001, 4326,
                                     MDSYS.SDO_POINT_TYPE(
                                         r.WGS84_LONGITUDE,
                                         r.WGS84_LATITUDE,
                                         NULL
                                     ), NULL, NULL
                                 )
                             )
                             RETURNING CLOB
                         )
                  FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS r
                  WHERE r.ANOMALY_FLAG = 1
                    AND r.WGS84_LONGITUDE IS NOT NULL
                    AND r.WGS84_LATITUDE IS NOT NULL~';
              COMMIT;
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_tables WHERE table_name = 'TREE_ANOMALY_RUNS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE TREE_ANOMALY_RUNS (
                      RUN_ID                 VARCHAR2(32) PRIMARY KEY,
                      SPECIES_NAME           VARCHAR2(254 CHAR) NOT NULL,
                      OUTLIER_RATE           NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_DATA_OBJECT_ID  NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_ROW_COUNT       NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SOURCE_MAX_SCN         NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      SCORED_COUNT           NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      FLAGGED_COUNT          NUMBER NOT NULL,
                      CREATED_AT             TIMESTAMP DEFAULT SYSTIMESTAMP
                  )~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_tables WHERE table_name = 'TREE_ANOMALY_SETTINGS';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE TABLE TREE_ANOMALY_SETTINGS (
                      SETTING_NAME  VARCHAR2(30),
                      SETTING_VALUE VARCHAR2(4000)
                  )~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_objects
          WHERE object_name = 'TREE_ANOMALY_INPUT_V'
            AND object_type = 'VIEW' AND status = 'VALID';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW TREE_ANOMALY_INPUT_V AS
                  SELECT SOURCE_RECORD_ID, TREE_AGE, TRUNK_DIAMETER
                  FROM BOMEN_TREES
                  WHERE SRT_WETENS = 'Quercus robur'
                    AND SOURCE_RECORD_ID IS NOT NULL
                    AND TREE_AGE IS NOT NULL
                    AND TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NOT NULL~';
          END IF;

          SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_count
          FROM user_objects
          WHERE object_name = 'TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS_V'
            AND object_type = 'VIEW' AND status = 'VALID';
          IF v_count = 0 THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  CREATE OR REPLACE VIEW TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS_V AS
                  SELECT RUN_ID, SOURCE_RECORD_ID, SPECIES_NAME, TREE_AGE,
                         TRUNK_DIAMETER, ANOMALY_FLAG, ANOMALY_PROBABILITY,
                         WGS84_LONGITUDE, WGS84_LATITUDE, CREATED_AT
                  FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS~';
          END IF;
      END prepare_tree_anomaly_storage;

      /

      ----

      -- Procedure PREPARE_TREE_ANOMALY_STORAGE compiled


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:00.046
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 2. Agent-callable model and scoring function

      One-class SVM uses TREE_AGE as numeric and TRUNK_DIAMETER as categorical.
      It has no target column. Oracle predicts 0 for an anomaly and 1 for a
      typical case. The outlier rate defaults to 0.01 (about 1% expected, not
      a guarantee); it is an explicit input so a different rate creates a new
      run. The same source signature and rate reuse saved results.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION tree_anomaly_agent_fn (
          p_species       IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT NULL,
          p_outlier_rate  IN NUMBER   DEFAULT NULL,
          p_force_refresh IN VARCHAR2 DEFAULT 'N'
      ) RETURN CLOB AS
          PRAGMA AUTONOMOUS_TRANSACTION;

          v_species        VARCHAR2(254) := NVL(TRIM(p_species), 'Quercus robur');
          v_rate           NUMBER := NVL(p_outlier_rate, 0.01);
          v_force          VARCHAR2(1) := UPPER(NVL(TRIM(p_force_refresh), 'N'));
          v_data_object_id NUMBER;
          v_source_count   NUMBER;
          v_source_scn     NUMBER;
          v_usable_count   NUMBER;
          v_final_count    NUMBER;
          v_final_scn      NUMBER;
          v_model_count    NUMBER;
          v_saved_count    NUMBER;
          v_scored_count   NUMBER;
          v_flagged_count  NUMBER;
          v_mappable_count NUMBER;
          v_map_count      NUMBER;
          v_run_id         VARCHAR2(32);
          v_reused         VARCHAR2(1) := 'N';
          v_top_flags      CLOB;
          v_response       CLOB;
      BEGIN
          IF UPPER(v_species) <> 'QUERCUS ROBUR' THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20101,
                  'This pilot supports Quercus robur only.');
          END IF;
          v_species := 'Quercus robur';

          IF v_rate <= 0 OR v_rate >= 1 THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20102,
                  'Outlier rate must be greater than 0 and less than 1.');
          END IF;
          IF v_force NOT IN ('Y', 'N') THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20103,
                  'p_force_refresh must be Y or N.');
          END IF;

          -- This function prepares its own tables/views; the user does not.
          prepare_tree_anomaly_storage;

          SELECT data_object_id INTO v_data_object_id
          FROM user_objects
          WHERE object_name = 'BOMEN_TREES' AND object_type = 'TABLE';

          SELECT COUNT(*), NVL(MAX(ORA_ROWSCN), 0),
                 COUNT(CASE WHEN SOURCE_RECORD_ID IS NOT NULL
                              AND TREE_AGE IS NOT NULL
                              AND TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NOT NULL THEN 1 END)
            INTO v_source_count, v_source_scn, v_usable_count
            FROM BOMEN_TREES
           WHERE SRT_WETENS = v_species;

          IF v_usable_count < 100 THEN
              RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20104,
                  'Fewer than 100 complete records for this species.');
          END IF;

          -- A READY run is reusable only if its saved rows still exist.
          IF v_force = 'N' THEN
              BEGIN
                  EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                      SELECT RUN_ID, SCORED_COUNT, FLAGGED_COUNT
                      FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RUNS
                      WHERE SPECIES_NAME = :species
                        AND OUTLIER_RATE = :rate
                        AND SOURCE_DATA_OBJECT_ID = :object_id
                        AND SOURCE_ROW_COUNT = :row_count
                        AND SOURCE_MAX_SCN = :source_scn
                      ORDER BY CREATED_AT DESC
                      FETCH FIRST 1 ROW ONLY~'
                  INTO v_run_id, v_scored_count, v_flagged_count
                  USING v_species, v_rate, v_data_object_id,
                        v_source_count, v_source_scn;

                  EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                      SELECT COUNT(*) FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS
                      WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~'
                  INTO v_saved_count USING v_run_id;

                  IF v_saved_count = v_scored_count
                     AND v_scored_count = v_usable_count THEN
                      v_reused := 'Y';
                  END IF;
              EXCEPTION
                  WHEN NO_DATA_FOUND THEN NULL;
              END;
          END IF;

          IF v_reused = 'N' THEN
              -- Only this pilot model and its settings are replaced. Previous
              -- RUN_IDs and scored rows remain available for audit/map use.
              SELECT COUNT(*) INTO v_model_count
              FROM user_mining_models
              WHERE model_name = 'TREE_QUERCUS_OCSVM_MODEL';
              IF v_model_count > 0 THEN
                  DBMS_DATA_MINING.DROP_MODEL('TREE_QUERCUS_OCSVM_MODEL');
              END IF;

              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE 'DELETE FROM TREE_ANOMALY_SETTINGS';
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE
                  'INSERT INTO TREE_ANOMALY_SETTINGS VALUES (:1, :2)'
                  USING DBMS_DATA_MINING.ALGO_NAME,
                        DBMS_DATA_MINING.ALGO_SUPPORT_VECTOR_MACHINES;
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE
                  'INSERT INTO TREE_ANOMALY_SETTINGS VALUES (:1, :2)'
                  USING DBMS_DATA_MINING.SVMS_OUTLIER_RATE,
                        TO_CHAR(v_rate, 'FM0D999999',
                                'NLS_NUMERIC_CHARACTERS=.,');
              COMMIT;

              DBMS_DATA_MINING.CREATE_MODEL(
                  model_name          => 'TREE_QUERCUS_OCSVM_MODEL',
                  mining_function     => DBMS_DATA_MINING.CLASSIFICATION,
                  data_table_name     => 'TREE_ANOMALY_INPUT_V',
                  case_id_column_name => 'SOURCE_RECORD_ID',
                  settings_table_name => 'TREE_ANOMALY_SETTINGS'
              );

              v_run_id := RAWTOHEX(SYS_GUID());
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  INSERT INTO TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS (
                      RUN_ID, SOURCE_RECORD_ID, SPECIES_NAME, TREE_AGE,
                      TRUNK_DIAMETER, ANOMALY_FLAG, ANOMALY_PROBABILITY,
                      WGS84_LONGITUDE, WGS84_LATITUDE, GEOMETRY
                  )
                  SELECT :run_id, s.SOURCE_RECORD_ID, s.SRT_WETENS,
                         s.TREE_AGE, s.TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                         CASE WHEN s.PREDICTED_CLASS = 0 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END,
                         s.ANOMALY_PROBABILITY,
                         s.WGS84_LONGITUDE, s.WGS84_LATITUDE, s.GEOMETRY
                  FROM (
                      SELECT b.SOURCE_RECORD_ID, b.SRT_WETENS,
                             b.TREE_AGE, b.TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                             b.WGS84_LONGITUDE, b.WGS84_LATITUDE, b.GEOMETRY,
                             PREDICTION(TREE_QUERCUS_OCSVM_MODEL USING
                                 b.TREE_AGE AS TREE_AGE,
                                 b.TRUNK_DIAMETER AS TRUNK_DIAMETER
                             ) AS PREDICTED_CLASS,
                             PREDICTION_PROBABILITY(
                                 TREE_QUERCUS_OCSVM_MODEL, 0 USING
                                 b.TREE_AGE AS TREE_AGE,
                                 b.TRUNK_DIAMETER AS TRUNK_DIAMETER
                             ) AS ANOMALY_PROBABILITY
                      FROM BOMEN_TREES b
                      WHERE b.SRT_WETENS = 'Quercus robur'
                        AND b.SOURCE_RECORD_ID IS NOT NULL
                        AND b.TREE_AGE IS NOT NULL
                        AND b.TRUNK_DIAMETER IS NOT NULL
                  ) s~'
              USING v_run_id;

              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  SELECT COUNT(*),
                         SUM(CASE WHEN ANOMALY_FLAG = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
                  FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id~'
              INTO v_scored_count, v_flagged_count USING v_run_id;

              -- Never publish a READY run if the source changed while scoring.
              SELECT COUNT(*), NVL(MAX(ORA_ROWSCN), 0)
                INTO v_final_count, v_final_scn
                FROM BOMEN_TREES WHERE SRT_WETENS = v_species;
              IF v_final_count <> v_source_count
                 OR v_final_scn <> v_source_scn THEN
                  RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(-20105,
                      'BOMEN_TREES changed during scoring. Retry the request.');
              END IF;

              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  INSERT INTO TREE_ANOMALY_RUNS (
                      RUN_ID, SPECIES_NAME, OUTLIER_RATE,
                      SOURCE_DATA_OBJECT_ID, SOURCE_ROW_COUNT, SOURCE_MAX_SCN,
                      SCORED_COUNT, FLAGGED_COUNT
                  ) VALUES (:1, :2, :3, :4, :5, :6, :7, :8)~'
              USING v_run_id, v_species, v_rate, v_data_object_id,
                    v_source_count, v_source_scn,
                    v_scored_count, v_flagged_count;
              COMMIT;
          END IF;

          -- Backfill cached runs too. Retraining is unnecessary for map recovery.
          EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
              SELECT COUNT(*) FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS
              WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id AND ANOMALY_FLAG = 1
                AND WGS84_LONGITUDE IS NOT NULL
                AND WGS84_LATITUDE IS NOT NULL~'
          INTO v_mappable_count USING v_run_id;

          EXECUTE IMMEDIATE
              'SELECT COUNT(*) FROM AGENT_MAP_RESULTS WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id'
          INTO v_map_count USING v_run_id;

          IF v_map_count <> v_mappable_count THEN
              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE
                  'DELETE FROM AGENT_MAP_RESULTS WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id'
              USING v_run_id;

              EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
                  INSERT INTO AGENT_MAP_RESULTS
                      (RUN_ID, FEATURE_ORDER, FEATURE_JSON)
                  SELECT r.RUN_ID,
                         ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
                             ORDER BY r.ANOMALY_PROBABILITY DESC NULLS LAST,
                                      r.SOURCE_RECORD_ID
                         ),
                         JSON_OBJECT(
                             'RUN_ID' VALUE r.RUN_ID,
                             'SOURCE_RECORD_ID' VALUE r.SOURCE_RECORD_ID,
                             'SPECIES_NAME' VALUE r.SPECIES_NAME,
                             'TREE_AGE' VALUE r.TREE_AGE,
                             'TRUNK_DIAMETER' VALUE r.TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                             'ANOMALY_PROBABILITY' VALUE r.ANOMALY_PROBABILITY,
                             'GEOJSON' VALUE SDO_UTIL.TO_GEOJSON(
                                 MDSYS.SDO_GEOMETRY(
                                     2001, 4326,
                                     MDSYS.SDO_POINT_TYPE(
                                         r.WGS84_LONGITUDE,
                                         r.WGS84_LATITUDE,
                                         NULL
                                     ), NULL, NULL
                                 )
                             )
                             RETURNING CLOB
                         )
                  FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS r
                  WHERE r.RUN_ID = :run_id
                    AND r.ANOMALY_FLAG = 1
                    AND r.WGS84_LONGITUDE IS NOT NULL
                    AND r.WGS84_LATITUDE IS NOT NULL~'
              USING v_run_id;
              COMMIT;
          END IF;

          EXECUTE IMMEDIATE q'~
              SELECT JSON_ARRAYAGG(
                         JSON_OBJECT(
                             'source_record_id' VALUE SOURCE_RECORD_ID,
                             'tree_age' VALUE TREE_AGE,
                             'trunk_diameter' VALUE TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                             'anomaly_probability' VALUE ANOMALY_PROBABILITY,
                             'longitude' VALUE WGS84_LONGITUDE,
                             'latitude' VALUE WGS84_LATITUDE
                             RETURNING CLOB
                         )
                         ORDER BY ANOMALY_PROBABILITY DESC
                         RETURNING CLOB
                     )
              FROM (
                  SELECT SOURCE_RECORD_ID, TREE_AGE, TRUNK_DIAMETER,
                         ANOMALY_PROBABILITY,
                         WGS84_LONGITUDE, WGS84_LATITUDE
                  FROM TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS
                  WHERE RUN_ID = :run_id AND ANOMALY_FLAG = 1
                  ORDER BY ANOMALY_PROBABILITY DESC, SOURCE_RECORD_ID
                  FETCH FIRST 10 ROWS ONLY
              )~'
          INTO v_top_flags USING v_run_id;

          IF v_top_flags IS NULL THEN
              v_top_flags := TO_CLOB('[]');
          END IF;

          SELECT JSON_OBJECT(
                     'status' VALUE 'success',
                     'run_id' VALUE v_run_id,
                     'species' VALUE v_species,
                     'outlier_rate' VALUE v_rate,
                     'source_trees' VALUE v_source_count,
                     'scored_trees' VALUE v_scored_count,
                     'flagged_trees' VALUE v_flagged_count,
                     'cache_reused' VALUE v_reused,
                     'top_flags' VALUE v_top_flags FORMAT JSON
                     RETURNING CLOB
                 )
            INTO v_response FROM dual;
          RETURN v_response;
      EXCEPTION
          WHEN OTHERS THEN
              ROLLBACK;
              RAISE;
      END tree_anomaly_agent_fn;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 3. Add the anomaly worker to the existing supervised team

      Keep TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM as the only active tree team. This section
      removes the old separate anomaly team if present, replaces anomaly-only
      metadata, and recreates the shared density supervisor with two worker
      choices. Saved density and anomaly result rows are not dropped. The team
      is briefly unavailable between DROP_TEAM and CREATE_TEAM; run these
      definition cells together when no request is in progress.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TEAM('TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_AGENT('TREE_ANOMALY_SUPERVISOR', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_AGENT('TREE_ANOMALY_AGENT', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TASK('TREE_ANOMALY_TASK', force => TRUE);
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_TOOL('TREE_ANOMALY_TOOL', force => TRUE);
      END;

      /
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TOOL(
              tool_name => 'TREE_ANOMALY_TOOL',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "function": "TREE_ANOMALY_AGENT_FN",
                  "instruction": "For Quercus robur only, reuse or rebuild the saved one-class SVM anomaly run. Return measured values from the function. A flag requests record review, not a health diagnosis.",
                  "tool_inputs": [
                      {"name":"p_species","description":"Optional species. This pilot accepts Quercus robur only; null uses Quercus robur."},
                      {"name":"p_outlier_rate","description":"Optional expected anomaly fraction between 0 and 1. Null uses 0.01."},
                      {"name":"p_force_refresh","description":"Y rebuilds even when the source signature matches; otherwise N."}
                  ]
              }~',
              description => 'Saves species-specific SVM anomaly flags and reuses unchanged runs.'
          );
      END;

      /


      -- PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:00.046
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >-
      -- DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TASK: TREE_ANOMALY_TASK

      DECLARE
          v_instruction VARCHAR2(4000) := q'|
      Answer the user's unusual-tree-record question: {query}


      1. This pilot supports only Quercus robur in BOMEN_TREES.

      2. Call TREE_ANOMALY_TOOL exactly once for a supported request.

      3. Use the user's outlier rate if stated; otherwise pass null (default
      0.01).

      4. Force refresh only when the user requests a rebuild; otherwise pass N.

      5. Report only measured counts, IDs, attributes, and locations in the tool
      JSON.

      6. Say that a flag means review the record, not that the tree is
      unhealthy.

      7. The tool saves flagged tree points for the map. Do not claim the
      browser map rendered unless the application confirms it.

      |';
          v_attributes CLOB;
      BEGIN
          SELECT JSON_OBJECT(
                     'instruction' VALUE v_instruction,
                     'tools' VALUE JSON_ARRAY('TREE_ANOMALY_TOOL') FORMAT JSON
                     RETURNING CLOB
                 ) INTO v_attributes FROM dual;
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TASK(
              task_name   => 'TREE_ANOMALY_TASK',
              attributes  => v_attributes,
              description => 'Reviews unusual age and diameter combinations for Quercus robur.'
          );
      END;

      /

      -- PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:00.037
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >-
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_AGENT(
              agent_name => 'TREE_ANOMALY_AGENT',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "profile_name": "OCI_GROK_4_3_BOMEN_BURRT_PROFILE",
                  "role": "You are a tree-record anomaly worker. Follow TREE_ANOMALY_TASK and report only measured data; do not infer tree health."
              }~',
              description => 'One-class SVM anomaly worker.'
          );
      END;

      /

      -- PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:00.051
    languageId: oracle-sql
  - kind: 2
    value: >
      BEGIN
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.DROP_AGENT(
              'TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR', force => TRUE
          );
          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_AGENT(
              agent_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "profile_name": "OCI_GROK_4_3_BOMEN_BURRT_PROFILE",
                  "role": "You supervise one Den Haag tree team. For neighbourhood tree-density or green-area questions, delegate to TREE_DENSITY_AGENT with TREE_DENSITY_TASK. For unusual recorded age and trunk-diameter combinations in Quercus robur, delegate to TREE_ANOMALY_AGENT with TREE_ANOMALY_TASK. For greetings, briefly describe both supported question types. Delegate only the relevant worker for a single-topic request; for a combined request, call each relevant worker once and distinguish their results. Report only measured tool results. An anomaly flag means record review, not poor tree health. Never claim the browser map rendered unless the application confirms it. Explain that the anomaly pilot supports Quercus robur only.",
                  "supervisor": true
              }~',
              description => 'Routes density and anomaly questions to specialist workers.'
          );

          DBMS_CLOUD_AI_AGENT.CREATE_TEAM(
              team_name => 'TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM',
              attributes => q'~{
                  "process": "sequential",
                  "supervisor_agent": "TREE_DENSITY_SUPERVISOR",
                  "agents": [
                      {"name": "TREE_DENSITY_AGENT", "task": "TREE_DENSITY_TASK"},
                      {"name": "TREE_ANOMALY_AGENT", "task": "TREE_ANOMALY_TASK"}
                  ]
              }~',
              description => 'One supervised team for tree density and anomaly review.'
          );
      END;

      /


      -- PL/SQL procedure successfully completed.


      -- Elapsed: 00:00:00.981
